From 073dade145dd2b37c8f2aa89080deec25e411b15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 16:45:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] chore(design): install the Design System Agent for the
 whole frontend

Installed with the agent's install.sh (Sep 30 version: lite mode, tools
do the checking):
- .claude/skills/design-agent (core skill, critic, references),
  .claude/design-agent/{tools,schemas,templates}, and the design-lead /
  design-critic agents.
- .claude/settings.json: SessionStart shows every design's stage; before
  the first edit to a UI file the owning design's decisions are shown;
  after each edit the token lint sends off-token values back.
- .gitignore tracks these (like .claude/gates/) so every checkout and
  worktree gets them; per-session hook state stays ignored.
- design-system-manifest.yaml (Fuji, harness.mode lite, text styles and
  spacing roles) and design-index.yaml at the root. Every UI file now has
  an owning design: nine designs incl. GFE-FUJI for the primitives.
- CLAUDE.md starts with the manifest version stamp and ends with the
  generated Fuji section; the team guide above it is unchanged.
- docs/design/agent/: the GFE-SORT records and the standalone audits,
  critique and tool results of every pre-existing page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
